From ccae23010861223807c40a879c50437d05c72d59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:34:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/21] ndb/cs: don't cut errors to 63 bytes

rwrite() read the error of a failed lookup into curerr[64], and
sendmsg() prefixes it with "cs: ". For a long name the reason got lost:

	cs: can't translate address no-such-host-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz

instead of "... .invalid: dns: name does not exist", so programs that
look at the error ("does not exist") cannot tell a missing name from
other failures. Use ERRMAX, as the rest of cs does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/src/cmd/ndb/cs.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/src/cmd/ndb/cs.c b/sys/src/cmd/ndb/cs.c
index 23d253d08..6718b3769 100644
--- a/sys/src/cmd/ndb/cs.c
+++ b/sys/src/cmd/ndb/cs.c
@@ -775,7 +775,7 @@ rwrite(Job *job, Mfile *mf)
 	int cnt, n;
 	char *err;
 	char *field[4];
-	char curerr[64];
+	char curerr[ERRMAX];
 
 	err = nil;
 	cnt = job->request.count;
